{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":78835,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"7029b0e3-ee46-5bc0-9cab-401ec4c54c48","total_cost_usd":0.633027,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12089,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7696,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12089,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7696,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12089},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6342,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006427,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7696,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12089,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6266,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-k1-reviewer-fable-48\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:f92b9f626c90493a67ec\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The workflow collapses the four repeated campaign rows of each mesocosm into a single seasonal mean before any statistical procedure, keyed by the declared independent-unit column mesocosm_id, so each independent unit enters the test exactly once.\",\"observed_value\":\"collapse_to_mesocosms averages float(record[FLUX_COLUMN]) values per mesocosm_id via statistics.fmean, yielding 24 collapsed values\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":32,\"end_line\":45,\"quoted_text\":\"def collapse_to_mesocosms(records):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Average each mesocosm's repeated campaigns into a single analysed value.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    series = OrderedDict()\\n    treatments = {}\\n    for record in records:\\n        unit = record[UNIT_COLUMN]\\n        group = record[GROUP_COLUMN]\\n        if treatments.setdefault(unit, group) != group:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"mesocosm \\\" + unit + \\\" carries two treatment labels\\\")\\n        series.setdefault(unit, []).append(float(record[FLUX_COLUMN]))\\n    collapsed = OrderedDict()\\n    for unit, fluxes in series.items():\\n        collapsed[unit] = (treatments[unit], statistics.fmean(fluxes), len(fluxes))\\n    return collapsed\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":19,\"end_line\":19,\"quoted_text\":\"UNIT_COLUMN = \\\"mesocosm_id\\\"\"}]},{\"description\":\"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied to the collapsed per-mesocosm means (12 warmed vs 12 ambient), not to the 96 campaign rows; group_means draws one value per entry of the collapsed OrderedDict, which is keyed by mesocosm_id.\",\"observed_value\":\"mannwhitneyu(warmed, ambient) where warmed and ambient are lists of mesocosm-level means\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":48,\"end_line\":50,\"quoted_text\":\"def group_means(collapsed, label):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Mesocosm-level means for one treatment arm, one value per mesocosm.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [mean for treatment, mean, _ in collapsed.values() if treatment == label]\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":59,\"end_line\":64,\"quoted_text\":\"    ambient = group_means(collapsed, AMBIENT)\\n    warmed = group_means(collapsed, WARMED)\\n    if len(ambient) + len(warmed) != len(collapsed):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"unexpected treatment label in the campaign file\\\")\\n\\n    outcome = mannwhitneyu(warmed, ambient, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\", method=\\\"exact\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected result states the test was run on 24 mesocosm-level values with one analysed value per mesocosm, and the reported U = 141.0 is only attainable on a 12-vs-12 comparison (maximum U = 144). Independent recomputation of the seasonal means from data/input.csv gives exactly three warmed-ambient inversions (ambient M12 mean 3.35 exceeds warmed M13 2.95, M14 3.10, M15 3.22), reproducing U = 144 - 3 = 141; a row-level 48-vs-48 test would produce U on a scale up to 2304.\",\"observed_value\":\"U = 141.0, p = 5.177e-06 on n = 12 + 12 mesocosm means; recomputed U = 141 matches\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":29,\"end_line\":29,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on 24 mesocosm-level mean CH4 fluxes (12 warmed vs 12 ambient, one analysed value per mesocosm): U = 141.0, p = 5.177e-06; warmed mesocosms released more methane (median mesocosm mean 3.82 vs 1.97 mg CH4 per square metre per hour).\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":13,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"The four campaign records of a mesocosm are repeated measurements of the same randomised\\nunit, so they were averaged before any test was run. Collapsing the long-format file gives\\n24 mesocosm mean CH4 fluxes, exactly one per mesocosm, so no mesocosm contributes more\\nthan one value. The 12 warmed mesocosm means were then compared with the 12 ambient\\nmesocosm means using a two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U test.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's conclusion is scoped to the independent unit (mesocosms), matching the unit declared in the data description, and explicitly states the 96 campaign rows were used only to estimate each mesocosm's seasonal mean.\",\"observed_value\":\"claim scoped to mesocosms; campaign rows used only for within-unit averaging\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":33,\"end_line\":36,\"quoted_text\":\"The comparison is between mesocosms, so it supports a claim about mesocosms rather than\\nabout individual chamber campaigns; the 96 campaign records were used only to estimate\\neach mesocosm's seasonal mean flux. Within-season variation is folded into that mean and\\nis not modelled separately, and the array covers one thaw season at a single fen.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one static-chamber methane flux measurement of one peat mesocosm on one campaign\\nIndependent unit column: mesocosm_id\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The precondition for the issue class is present in the raw data: every mesocosm appears four times in data/input.csv (96 rows for 24 mesocosms), so an analysis that fed rows directly into a row-independent test would have committed the issue. This raises the hazard but does not demonstrate it, because the workflow collapses the repeats before testing.\",\"observed_value\":\"96 data rows, 24 mesocosms, 4 campaigns each; e.g. M01 appears at weeks 3, 6, 9 and 12\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"(weeks 3, 6, 9 and 12), so every mesocosm appears in the file four times, once per\\ncampaign. The file is stored campaign by campaign: all 24 mesocosms for week 3, then all\\n24 for week 6, and so on, giving 96 rows.\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"M01,1,ambient,3,1.14,7.4\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":74,\"end_line\":74,\"quoted_text\":\"M01,1,ambient,12,1.30,9.0\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to show that the test was actually run on the 96 campaign rows despite the report's claims. Tracing the code, mannwhitneyu receives the outputs of group_means, which iterates over the collapsed OrderedDict keyed by mesocosm_id (24 entries), so the test inputs cannot contain more than one value per mesocosm; the code also raises on inconsistent treatment labels or unbalanced campaign counts. As a numerical check independent of the code's claims, I recomputed all 24 seasonal means from data/input.csv by hand and counted warmed-ambient pair inversions: ambient M12 (mean 3.35) exceeds warmed M13 (2.95), M14 (3.10) and M15 (3.22), and no other inversions exist, giving U = 12*12 - 3 = 141, exactly matching the reported U = 141.0. A row-level 48-vs-48 test would yield U on a 0-2304 scale, so the reported statistic is inconsistent with a row-level analysis. The falsification attempt failed; the analysis is genuinely mesocosm-level.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k1-reviewer-fable-48","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:f92b9f626c90493a67ec","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses the four repeated campaign rows of each mesocosm into a single seasonal mean before any statistical procedure, keyed by the declared independent-unit column mesocosm_id, so each independent unit enters the test exactly once.","observed_value":"collapse_to_mesocosms averages float(record[FLUX_COLUMN]) values per mesocosm_id via statistics.fmean, yielding 24 collapsed values","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":32,"end_line":45,"quoted_text":"def collapse_to_mesocosms(records):\n    \"\"\"Average each mesocosm's repeated campaigns into a single analysed value.\"\"\"\n    series = OrderedDict()\n    treatments = {}\n    for record in records:\n        unit = record[UNIT_COLUMN]\n        group = record[GROUP_COLUMN]\n        if treatments.setdefault(unit, group) != group:\n            raise ValueError(\"mesocosm \" + unit + \" carries two treatment labels\")\n        series.setdefault(unit, []).append(float(record[FLUX_COLUMN]))\n    collapsed = OrderedDict()\n    for unit, fluxes in series.items():\n        collapsed[unit] = (treatments[unit], statistics.fmean(fluxes), len(fluxes))\n    return collapsed"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":19,"end_line":19,"quoted_text":"UNIT_COLUMN = \"mesocosm_id\""}]},{"description":"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied to the collapsed per-mesocosm means (12 warmed vs 12 ambient), not to the 96 campaign rows; group_means draws one value per entry of the collapsed OrderedDict, which is keyed by mesocosm_id.","observed_value":"mannwhitneyu(warmed, ambient) where warmed and ambient are lists of mesocosm-level means","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":48,"end_line":50,"quoted_text":"def group_means(collapsed, label):\n    \"\"\"Mesocosm-level means for one treatment arm, one value per mesocosm.\"\"\"\n    return [mean for treatment, mean, _ in collapsed.values() if treatment == label]"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":59,"end_line":64,"quoted_text":"    ambient = group_means(collapsed, AMBIENT)\n    warmed = group_means(collapsed, WARMED)\n    if len(ambient) + len(warmed) != len(collapsed):\n        raise ValueError(\"unexpected treatment label in the campaign file\")\n\n    outcome = mannwhitneyu(warmed, ambient, alternative=\"two-sided\", method=\"exact\")"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result states the test was run on 24 mesocosm-level values with one analysed value per mesocosm, and the reported U = 141.0 is only attainable on a 12-vs-12 comparison (maximum U = 144). Independent recomputation of the seasonal means from data/input.csv gives exactly three warmed-ambient inversions (ambient M12 mean 3.35 exceeds warmed M13 2.95, M14 3.10, M15 3.22), reproducing U = 144 - 3 = 141; a row-level 48-vs-48 test would produce U on a scale up to 2304.","observed_value":"U = 141.0, p = 5.177e-06 on n = 12 + 12 mesocosm means; recomputed U = 141 matches","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":29,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test on 24 mesocosm-level mean CH4 fluxes (12 warmed vs 12 ambient, one analysed value per mesocosm): U = 141.0, p = 5.177e-06; warmed mesocosms released more methane (median mesocosm mean 3.82 vs 1.97 mg CH4 per square metre per hour)."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"The four campaign records of a mesocosm are repeated measurements of the same randomised\nunit, so they were averaged before any test was run. Collapsing the long-format file gives\n24 mesocosm mean CH4 fluxes, exactly one per mesocosm, so no mesocosm contributes more\nthan one value. The 12 warmed mesocosm means were then compared with the 12 ambient\nmesocosm means using a two-sided exact Mann-Whitney U test."}]},{"description":"The report's conclusion is scoped to the independent unit (mesocosms), matching the unit declared in the data description, and explicitly states the 96 campaign rows were used only to estimate each mesocosm's seasonal mean.","observed_value":"claim scoped to mesocosms; campaign rows used only for within-unit averaging","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":33,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"The comparison is between mesocosms, so it supports a claim about mesocosms rather than\nabout individual chamber campaigns; the 96 campaign records were used only to estimate\neach mesocosm's seasonal mean flux. Within-season variation is folded into that mean and\nis not modelled separately, and the array covers one thaw season at a single fen."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"One row is: one static-chamber methane flux measurement of one peat mesocosm on one campaign\nIndependent unit column: mesocosm_id"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The precondition for the issue class is present in the raw data: every mesocosm appears four times in data/input.csv (96 rows for 24 mesocosms), so an analysis that fed rows directly into a row-independent test would have committed the issue. This raises the hazard but does not demonstrate it, because the workflow collapses the repeats before testing.","observed_value":"96 data rows, 24 mesocosms, 4 campaigns each; e.g. M01 appears at weeks 3, 6, 9 and 12","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":8,"end_line":10,"quoted_text":"(weeks 3, 6, 9 and 12), so every mesocosm appears in the file four times, once per\ncampaign. The file is stored campaign by campaign: all 24 mesocosms for week 3, then all\n24 for week 6, and so on, giving 96 rows."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"M01,1,ambient,3,1.14,7.4"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":74,"end_line":74,"quoted_text":"M01,1,ambient,12,1.30,9.0"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show that the test was actually run on the 96 campaign rows despite the report's claims. Tracing the code, mannwhitneyu receives the outputs of group_means, which iterates over the collapsed OrderedDict keyed by mesocosm_id (24 entries), so the test inputs cannot contain more than one value per mesocosm; the code also raises on inconsistent treatment labels or unbalanced campaign counts. As a numerical check independent of the code's claims, I recomputed all 24 seasonal means from data/input.csv by hand and counted warmed-ambient pair inversions: ambient M12 (mean 3.35) exceeds warmed M13 (2.95), M14 (3.10) and M15 (3.22), and no other inversions exist, giving U = 12*12 - 3 = 141, exactly matching the reported U = 141.0. A row-level 48-vs-48 test would yield U on a 0-2304 scale, so the reported statistic is inconsistent with a row-level analysis. The falsification attempt failed; the analysis is genuinely mesocosm-level.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":41614,"ttft_stream_ms":3144,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":77287,"uuid":"c178b732-a7fd-4803-9c66-7cbd624744f2"}
